WEBVTT

00:00:00.920 --> 00:00:05.200
Here is a beautiful ribber stitch pattern
that was inspired by a hand knitting

00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:07.840
pattern called Textured Rib.

00:00:07.920 --> 00:00:11.680
It's basically 2x2
ribbing, slipping the knit stitches

00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:14.440
to highlight the purl stitches.

00:00:14.520 --> 00:00:19.920
More attractive than plain old 2x2
ribbing, it looks great on both sides.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:22.800
I can't decide which side I like better.

00:00:22.880 --> 00:00:29.040
Instead of right and wrong side,
I'm calling these side A and side B.

00:00:29.120 --> 00:00:32.760
The pattern is worked over a standard
2x2 needle set up.

00:00:32.840 --> 00:00:36.760
Two needles on the ribber,
two needles on the main bed.

00:00:36.840 --> 00:00:40.920
Then stitches are slipped every other row.

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:46.760
I chose to slip on my ribber, keeping the
main bed needles in work on every row.

00:00:46.840 --> 00:00:51.640
Of course, you could do it the opposite
way, slipping on the main bed

00:00:51.720 --> 00:00:55.200
and knitting every row on the ribber.

00:00:56.200 --> 00:01:02.360
Now, notice the slip strands
on side B, adding interesting texture.

00:01:02.440 --> 00:01:04.640
I hope you'll give this
stitch pattern a try.

00:01:04.720 --> 00:01:08.880
If you've struggled with 2x2
ribbing, the cast on can be a bit

00:01:08.960 --> 00:01:10.480
of a challenge at first.

00:01:10.560 --> 00:01:14.240
We have an entire course
covering everything you need to know.

00:01:14.320 --> 00:01:15.720
Knititnow.

00:01:15.800 --> 00:01:17.560
com/2x2

00:01:18.360 --> 00:01:19.160
Happy Knitting.

